  "schema_findings": [
    "The current index intentionally indexes exact workspace-source bytes and candidate snapshots. All 33 canonical paths are historical_source labels rather than duplicate source aliases, so the old pins[canonical] lookup raises KeyError despite covered candidate bytes.",
    "run_files independently reconstructs each accepted workspace path from its module name and the frozen module plan. It binds workspace bytes to source_sha256 and records historical[workspace]=module_row.source. The raw-plan/index reconstruction preserves that historical_source label and checks complete equality with the supplied index.",
    "The v4 assertions require digest(canonical)=candidate.sha256, pins[workspace]=candidate.sha256, and historical[workspace]=canonical. Together with unchanged index and in-memory tar/member checks, this binds the canonical path, archived bytes and candidate source hash without requiring redundant aliases.",
    "The candidate and non-null before snapshot pins remain required. The 146 present pins, 16 absences, exact 33 overlays and changed-module set, no new retirements, exact profiles, 199 fresh triples, 2 audit triples, full 230 workspace providers, and exact prior eleven-file boundary checks are unchanged.",
    "Accepted candidate and mandatory failed /tmp/k215-phase23-check-v1 remain distinct. The failed prefix cannot supply a terminal accepted result; the original failed capture-reader outer receipt remains preserved separately from Lean mathematical/full-run failures.",
    "The repair changes only the reader. It does not modify archive, config, index, raw receipts, compiler inputs/results or previous phase22 leaf files; no recapture or proof rerun is logically required for this reader alias-assumption correction."
  ],
